    "content": [
     {
      "type": "thinking",
      "thinking": "I'm testing whether \"Merti\" could map to \"Mr.t-j\" (beloved one/my beloved) versus \"Mr.t-jt\" (beloved of the father) — the trailing t in the second option seems to be a radical consonant from \"father\" rather than a feminine ending, so it doesn't quite fit the name as spelled.\n\nI recall Merti is also listed as one of Thutmose III's foreign wives alongside Menwi and Menhet, likely a Semitic name rather than purely Egyptian, but sticking to the morphological rules, \"beloved one\" remains the better match.\n\n",
      "signature": ""
     }
    ],
